WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.230
When you take something out and do not put it back,

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.670
the situation changes.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.170
The second draw is from a different bag.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.890
To keep track, follow each possible route step by step.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.130
Using the original bag for both draws is a common error.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.510
Updating after each step is what makes the answer right.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.480
A bag holds two red counters and two blue counters.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.780
Draw two counters at random, one after the other,

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.790
without putting the first back.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.120
What is the probability that both are red?

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.320
Pause and think about the bag after the first draw.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.170
On the first draw, two of the four counters are red.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.690
The chance of red is two out of four, which is one half.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:47.430
If the first was red, the bag now has one red

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:48.280
and two blue.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.010
The chance of red again is one out of three.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.250
Along one route, multiply: one half times one third

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.220
is one sixth.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.480
So the probability of two reds is one sixth.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:01.620
Complete the tree.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:05.880
Red then blue is one half times two thirds, one third.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:08.500
Blue then red is also one third.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.840
Blue then blue is one sixth.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:13.900
The four routes add to one, which is a good check.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:16.780
What is the chance of one of each colour?

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.300
That happens on two different routes: red then blue,

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:21.560
or blue then red.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.950
Different routes are added: one third plus one third

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:25.960
is two thirds.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:29.400
Update the situation after each step.

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:31.160
Multiply along a route.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:32.360
Add separate routes.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.350
Notebook challenge: a bag has three red counters

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:36.520
and one blue.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.880
Two are drawn without replacement.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.300
What is the probability both are red?
